<title>AUSTRIA: Austria's Klestil suffering &quot;severe&quot; pneumonia.</title>
<headline>Austria's Klestil suffering &quot;severe&quot; pneumonia.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-09-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian President Thomas Klestil, in hospital since September 13, is suffering from a &quot;severe, aggressive and atypical strain of pneumonia&quot;, the presidential spokesman told Austrian news agency APA on Sunday.</p>
<p>Heinz Nussbaumer told APA that although there was a slight improvement in Klestil's condition it would take some time for him to recover.</p>
<p>All meetings have been cancelled for the next few days. Last week, 64-year-old Klestil had to cancel a two-day official visit to Germany where he was to meet German President Roman Herzog.</p>
</text>
